course: dictionary
lesson: 13570
title: Sounds you cannot hear
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word inaudible means too quiet to be heard. Look at its parts: in- means not, and audible means able to be heard. So inaudible means not able to be heard. «The bell rang, but its sound was inaudible from the far end of the field.» The bell was rung, yet nobody at the far end could hear it, so inaudible fits.
explain: Clues in the sentence help you find the meaning. Ask yourself: what would stop someone hearing a sound? Thick walls, a soft voice, or a long distance all make a sound hard to hear. «The music was inaudible through the thick walls» tells you the music was there, but too quiet to hear through the wall.
explain: You can check the meaning by swapping in your own words. Put «could not be heard» in place of inaudible. «Your answer was inaudible — speak up» becomes «Your answer could not be heard, so speak up.» That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Inaudible means too quiet to be heard.
fact: Inaudible is an adjective, so it describes a noun: «an inaudible whisper».
fact: The opposite of inaudible is audible, which means loud enough to be heard.
fact: «Your answer was inaudible — speak up» means your answer was too quiet for people to hear, so you should say it louder.
fact: The prefix in- means not, so inaudible means not able to be heard.
exercise: «The music was inaudible through the thick walls.» What does inaudible mean? | Hard to see | Very loud and clear | Brightly coloured | *Too quiet to be heard
exercise: Find and copy the word that means too quiet to be heard. | heard | loud | *inaudible | speak
exercise: Tom says, «Your answer was inaudible — speak up.» What does Tom want you to do? | Stop talking for the day | *Say your answer louder so people can hear it | Whisper even more | Sing your answer
test: «The rain was so light that the drumming on the roof was inaudible.» What does inaudible mean here? | Wet and cold | *Too quiet to be heard | Very loud | Bright and shiny
test: Which word means the opposite of inaudible? | Muffled | Faint | *Audible | Whispered
exam: «The clock ticked, but its ticks were inaudible over the noisy crowd.» What does inaudible mean? | Full of light | *Too quiet to be heard | Loud enough to hear | Very slow
